# ==============================================================================
# Portfolio-Supplier-Spend-Consolidation-Dashboard
# .gitignore — COMMITTED FIRST, ALONE, BEFORE ANY OTHER FILE EXISTS
#
# This repository is PUBLIC from creation. There is no private window in which a
# mistaken commit can be removed before anyone sees it. `.gitignore` does not
# apply to already-tracked paths, and `git rm --cached` is forward-looking only:
# every commit made before it still contains the blob.
#
# Governing rules: charter L-3 (raw register never committed) and Companies
# House Crown copyright condition 4 (data-protection responsibility rests with
# the publisher of the derived work).
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. RAW AND INTERMEDIATE DATA — the reason this file is committed first
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# data/raw/     ~470 MB Companies House register + 62 spend CSVs.
#               Registered addresses may be residential.
# data/interim/ No evidential value; regenerable.
#
# The `*` + negation pattern is deliberate: a bare `data/raw/` would also block
# the .gitkeep placeholder the scaffold needs.

data/raw/*
!data/raw/.gitkeep

data/interim/*
!data/interim/.gitkeep

# Belt and braces — these names must never appear anywhere in the tree,
# whatever directory someone puts them in.
BasicCompanyData*
BasicCompanyData*.zip
BasicCompanyData*.csv
**/companies_house/
**/companies-house/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. CREDENTIALS — narrow patterns, not blanket *.json
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# B-DS-04 (Contracts Finder) is published as OCDS JSON, and config files are
# JSON. A blanket *.json would hide real project files. These patterns target
# credential shapes specifically.

*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Google Cloud service-account keys
*service-account*.json
*service_account*.json
*-key.json
*_key.json
*credentials*.json
*client_secret*.json
gcloud-*.json
application_default_credentials.json
.gcloud/
.config/gcloud/

# BigQuery / gcloud local state
.bigqueryrc

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. TABLEAU — the .twbx is committed; extracts and backups are not
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# READ THIS BEFORE THE FIRST TABLEAU SAVE.
#
# `tableau/spend-consolidation.twbx` IS committed — it is the E-7 artefact.
# A .twbx is a PACKAGED workbook: it EMBEDS its data extract.
#
# .gitignore CANNOT protect you here, because the file is deliberately tracked.
# The guard is procedural: build the extract from data/outputs/ aggregates only,
# never from a full resolved or staging table. See the runbook §4.

*.hyper
*.tde
*.tdsx
*.twbr
*.twb.bak
tableau/Backup/
tableau/*.hyper
tableau/*.tde
tableau/Logs/
tableau/TableauTemp/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. PYTHON — acquisition and profiling scripts only (charter §4: Python is
#    allocated to Portfolio C; B uses it for acquisition, not analysis)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg

# Virtual environments
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/
env.bak/
venv.bak/

# Jupyter (not expected in B, ignored defensively)
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.ipynb_checkpoints

# Testing / coverage
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. LOCAL DATABASE ENGINES — B-5 DuckDB / SQLite, the approved local alternative
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# If the local path is ever exercised, its database file would contain the full
# Companies House register. Ignored in advance.

*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite-journal

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. LARGE / ARCHIVE FORMATS ANYWHERE IN THE TREE
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every legitimate committed artefact in this repo is .sql, .py, .md, .csv
# (small), .twbx or .png. Nothing needs to be a zip or a parquet.

*.zip
*.gz
*.tar
*.tgz
*.7z
*.rar
*.parquet
*.avro
*.orc

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 7. EDITOR AND OS NOISE
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 8. WHAT IS DELIBERATELY *NOT* IGNORED — do not add these
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# docs/provenance.csv        69 rows — the E-1 reproducibility record
# docs/review_queue.csv      tier-4 ambiguities, decisions blank
# docs/match_precision.md    the E-3 measurement
# data/outputs/*.csv         small derived aggregates, the Tableau source
# sql/**/*.sql               every layer
# scripts/*.py               acquisition and profiling
# tableau/*.twbx             the packaged workbook (see §3)
#
# If a future edit makes one of these ignored, E-1, E-3 or E-7 loses its
# evidence. Check `git status --ignored` after any change to this file.
